    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0232" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119 P 43/923: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Special
                        Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">House</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-20T19:00:00-05:00"
                            >November 20, 1918—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. For Auchincloss from Polk. Your 118, November 18.<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d146-f1"/> Department would like you to go ahead on the plan
                    outlined in your 99 with the modifications made by our Number 36.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d146-f2"/> Suggested that Strauss<anchor n="16" xml:id="d146-f3"/>
                    or Kent<anchor n="17" xml:id="d146-f4"/> be taken over as financial adviser …
                    President said he would telegraph for some one when he was needed. This seems to
                    be the plan they are following in regard to representatives of the various
                    boards. President and commissioners plan to sail about December 3d. Commission
                    has not yet been determined. Strictly confidentially, President taking with him
                    Cary Grayson<anchor n="18" xml:id="d146-f5"/> and Creel, not Tumulty.<anchor
                        n="19" xml:id="d146-f6"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d146-f1" n="14" xml:id="d146-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Post</hi>, <ref target="#pg197">p. 197</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d146-f2" n="15" xml:id="d146-f2-content">
                <p>No. 99 is printed on <ref target="#pg194">p. 194</ref>; No. 36, on <ref
                        target="#pg196">p. 196</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d146-f3" n="16" xml:id="d146-f3-content">
                <p> Albert Strauss, Vice Governor of the Federal Reserve Board.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d146-f4" n="17" xml:id="d146-f4-content">
                <p> William Kent, member of the United States Tariff Commission.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d146-f5" n="18" xml:id="d146-f5-content">
                <p>Rear Admiral Cary T. Grayson, physician to the President.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d146-f6" n="19" xml:id="d146-f6-content">
                <p> Joseph P. Tumulty, secretary to the President.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
